  "explains": "A line inside BalancesController.one changes. The controller is decorated @Controller({ path: \"balances\", version: \"1\" }) and src/main.ts enables URI versioning, so Nest puts the version in the path (without enableVersioning a version would add no segment, and with a header or media type versioning none either). The version is not evaluated. The route is GET /api/<unknown:version>/balances/{account}, flagged partial, and the run says so with route_path_partial at the controller decorator. The other method of the controller is not reached. The client URL BALANCES_URL, /api/ledger/balances, has one segment less than the route, so no http edge is claimed.",
